<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan ICBC Jan-Nov sales up 19.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Taiwan ICBC Jan-Nov sales up 19.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's International Commercial Bank of China (ICBC) said on Friday total sales revenue for the first eleven months of 1996 rose 19.5 percent to T$33.78 billion from T$28.267 billion in the same period in 1995.</p>
<p>For November alone, ICBC posted sales revenue of T$3.445 billion, up 21.07 percent from T$2.845 billion in November 1995, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>It did not give profit figures.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (5080815)</p>
</text>
